    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0476" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p1/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">775.5 MSP/11–352:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Ethiopia</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d189-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-11-14T18:07:00-05:00">November 14, 1952—6:07
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>268. Dept advised informally price list mil
                    equipment (Embtel 353, Nov 3)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d189-f2"/> being actively processed and shld be available approx two
                    weeks. Understand certain items required clarification by MA. When completed price list will be presented Ethio
                    Amb here and transmitted simultaneously to
                        MA.</p>
                <p>Dept also advised informally JCS comite has recommended JCS approve mil training assistance for Ethio army. Favorable action by JCS
                    and formal notification by Defense to State expected next week.</p>
                <p>Utter told Aklilou progress being made on
                    above matters and Aklilou probably
                    informed Emperor. If opportune you may confirm foregoing to Emperor emphasizing
                    final action not yet taken by USG.</p>
                <p>Aklilou and Spencer are not yet ready
                    conclude base agreement. We have impression they are stalling until after
                    discussion Eritrea item concluded in UNGA.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was drafted by Wellons and
                        Beard (AF).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f2" n="2" xml:id="d189-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it asked if the Department could tell the Embassy when the list of
                    equipment would be ready. (775.5 MSP/11–352)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
